<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for graph of a curve" class="sr-only"><ul>
<li>In quadrant 1:<br>
<ul>
<li>The curve begins at point (0 comma 1).</li>
<li>The curve rises sharply to point (2 comma 6).</li>
<li>The curve rises gradually to point (4 comma 7).</li>
<li>The curve rises gradually to point (6 comma 8).</li>
<li>The curve rises sharply and ends at point (8 comma 10).</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The graph shows the momentum <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>, in newton-seconds, of an object <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> seconds after the object started moving, for <math alttext="0 less than or equals x less than or equals 8"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. What is the average rate of change, in newton-seconds per second, in the momentum of the object from <math alttext="x equals 2"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>2</mn>
</mrow>
</math> to <math alttext="x equals 6"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>6</mn>
</mrow>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["0.5","1/2"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["0.5","1/2"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is&nbsp;<math alttext="one half"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. For the graph shown, <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> represents time, in seconds, and <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> represents momentum, in newton-seconds. Therefore, the average rate of change, in newton-seconds per second, in the momentum of the object between two <em>x</em>-values is the difference in the corresponding <em>y</em>-values divided by the difference in the <em>x</em>-values. The graph shows that at <math alttext="x equals 2"><mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>2</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, the corresponding <em>y</em>-value is <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math>. The graph also shows that at <math alttext="x equals 6"><mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>6</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, the corresponding <em>y</em>-value is <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math>. It follows that the average rate of change, in newton-seconds per second, from <math alttext="x equals 2"><mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>2</mn>
</mrow>
</math> to <math alttext="x equals 6"><mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>6</mn>
</mrow>
</math> is <math alttext="StartFraction 8 minus 6 Over 6 minus 2 EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, which is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext="two fourths"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="one half"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. Note that 1/2 and .5 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"9bb4107c","external_id":"71a3b42d-82b2-44f5-8a6d-50461b5cbd2f","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"234bb617-730d-44cc-a9eb-21eadfbaf4e7","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"285.138906pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 304.038906 285.138906\" width=\"304.038906pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Graph of a curve in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis is labeled Time, in seconds. It ranges from 0 to 9 in increments of 1. The y axis is labeled Momentum, in newton-seconds. It ranges from 0 to 11 in increments of 1. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 285.138906 \nL 304.038906 285.138906 \nL 304.038906 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 24.678906 260.46 \nL 296.838906 260.46 \nL 296.838906 10.98 \nL 24.678906 10.98 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\">\n  