</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"fb2a6fce-734e-4f01-867f-eafbd6585150","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing linear</p>"},{"id":"1f0d240f-1579-4720-80a7-b24faf4a531d","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing linear</p>"},{"id":"da4c70f3-2e86-4ae4-b5bf-804fc4e7e27a","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"ae0a49fd-a012-4b8c-bf33-84a64656fb77","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing exponential</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["1f0d240f-1579-4720-80a7-b24faf4a531d"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. The given values show that as <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> increases,&nbsp;<math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> also increases, which means that <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math> is an increasing function. Furthermore, <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> increases at a constant rate of <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> for each increase of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> by <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>. A function with a constant rate of change is linear. Thus, the function <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math> can be described as an increasing linear function.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. For a decreasing linear function, as <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> increases, <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> decreases rather than increases.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. For a decreasing exponential function, for each increase of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> by <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>, <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> decreases by a fixed percentage rather than increases at a constant rate.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. For an increasing exponential function, for each increase of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> by <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>, <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> increases by a fixed percentage rather than at a constant rate.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"a03b7e02","external_id":"4c22545c-b1dc-417e-a342-b8115c476ce0","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"d49542e0-30e3-4895-8dbf-f423bfc3cd6c","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The table shows selected values from function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<figure class=\"table\"><table border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3906px;\">\n<th style=\"width: 47.704%; text-align: center; height: 22.3906px;\" scope=\"col\"><math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math></th>\n<th style=\"width: 47.704%; text-align: center; height: 22.3906px;\" scope=\"col\"><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math></th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3906px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.704%; height: 22.3906px; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"negative 1\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn>\n</math></td>\n<td style=\"width: 47.704%; height: 22.3906px; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"16\"><mn>16</mn>\n</math></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3906px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.704%; height: 22.3906px; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math></td>\n<td style=\"width: 47.704%; height: 22.3906px; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3906px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.704%; height: 22.3906px; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math></td>\n<td style=\"width: 47.704%; height: