<p style="text-align: left;">How many more students were born in August than were born in July?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"dc7e9694-6396-4722-a964-cd200e3d2eca","content":"<p><math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d5b51fbc-be94-4610-b90d-d28447694b8a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"286ad461-0274-4401-a4c7-b856138e548d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"02ea02a4-ded3-46f8-9ff1-4aa8a465af98","content":"<p><math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["02ea02a4-ded3-46f8-9ff1-4aa8a465af98"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. It's given that the bar graph shows the number of students from one school who were born in either July, August, September, or October. The bar representing the number of students born in August has a height of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="50"><mn>50</mn></math>; therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="50"><mn>50</mn></math> students were born in August. The bar representing the number of students born in July has a height of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="40"><mn>40</mn></math>; therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="40"><mn>40</mn></math> students were born in July. Thus, there were <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="50 minus 40"><mn>50</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math> more students born in August than in July.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the total number of students born in July and August.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect. This is the number of students born in August.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the number of students born in July.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"a067c926","external_id":"ad801a2d-5e09-4c92-b37a-9c8b027d62f2","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"c7f6a085-b283-473c-93b7-dc08c62f0c5e","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.C.","skill_desc":"One-variable data: Distributions and measures of center and spread","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The bar graph shows the distribution of the number of students from one school who were born in one of four months.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"380\" height=\"383.6922607421875\" viewBox=\"0 0 380 383.6922607421875\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A bar graph. The horizontal axis is labeled Month. 4 bars are shown. The vertical axis is labeled Number of students. It ranges from 0 to 70 in increments of 10. Refer to long description.\"><g id=\"ed420550-79eb-48d4-af01-cd27cdd08af0\" data-name=\"Layer 1\"><defs>\n      <pattern id=\"bar4\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"10\" height=\"100\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" patternTransform=\"rotate(50)\">\n  \t\t<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"5\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#CDCDCD\"></rect>\n  \t\t<rect x=\"5\" y=\"0\" width=\"5\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#444444\"></rect>\n      </pattern>\n      </defs><line xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x1=\"79.359375\" y1=\"48\" x2=\"365\" y2=\"48\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></line><line xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x1=\"73.359375\" y1=\"48\" x2=\"85.359375\" y2=\"48\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></line><text te