g\" x1=\"79.359375\" y1=\"190.85714285714286\" x2=\"365\" y2=\"190.85714285714286\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></line><line xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x1=\"73.359375\" y1=\"190.85714285714286\" x2=\"85.359375\" y2=\"190.85714285714286\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></line><text text-anchor=\"end\" transform=\"translate(67.359375 196.85714285714286)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">20</text><line xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x1=\"79.359375\" y1=\"219.42857142857144\" x2=\"365\" y2=\"219.42857142857144\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></line><line xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x1=\"73.359375\" y1=\"219.42857142857144\" x2=\"85.359375\" y2=\"219.42857142857144\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></line><text text-anchor=\"end\" transform=\"translate(67.359375 225.42857142857144)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">10</text><line xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x1=\"79.359375\" y1=\"248\" x2=\"365\" y2=\"248\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></line><line xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x1=\"73.359375\" y1=\"248\" x2=\"85.359375\" y2=\"248\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></line><text text-anchor=\"end\" transform=\"translate(67.359375 254)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">0</text><text text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"translate(24 148) rotate(-90)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">Number of students</text><line xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x1=\"79.359375\" y1=\"48\" x2=\"79.359375\" y2=\"248\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></line><rect xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"111.09722222222223\" y=\"133.71428571428572\" height=\"114.28571428571428\" width=\"31.73784722222222\" fill=\"#B3B3B3\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"mitre\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></rect><text xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" text-anchor=\"end\" transform=\"translate(136.88614583333333 267.84) rotate(-40)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">July</text><rect xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"174.57291666666669\" y=\"105.14285714285714\" height=\"142.85714285714286\" width=\"31.73784722222222\" fill=\"#B3B3B3\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"mitre\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></rect><text xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" text-anchor=\"end\" transform=\"translate(200.3618402777778 267.84) rotate(-40)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">August</text><rect xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"238.04861111111114\" y=\"56.571428571428555\" height=\"191.42857142857144\" width=\"31.73784722222222\" fill=\"#B3B3B3\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"mitre\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></rect><text xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" text-anchor=\"end\" transform=\"translate(263.83753472222224 267.84) rotate(-40)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">September</text><rect xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"301.5243055555556\" y=\"99.42857142857142\" height=\"148.57142857142858\" width=\"31.73784722222222\" fill=\"#B3B3B3\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"mitre\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></rect><text xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" text-anchor=\"end\" transform=\"translate(327.31322916666676 267.84) rotate(-40)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">October</text><text text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"translate(222.1796875 24)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">   </text><text text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"translate(222.1796875 355.5322607421875)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">Month</text></g></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for bar graph\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>The Number of students data for the 4 bars are as follows:<br><ul><li>July: 40</li><li>August: 50</li><li>September: 67&nbsp;</li><li>October: 52</li></ul></li></ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">How many more students were born in August than were born in July?</p>","keys":["02ea02a4-ded3-46f8-9ff1-4aa8a465af98"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"dc7e9694-6396-4722-a964-cd200e3d2eca","content":"<p><math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d5b51fbc-be94-4610-b90d-d28447694b8a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"286ad461-0274-4401-a4c7-b856138e548d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"02ea02a4-ded3-46f8-9ff1-4aa8a465af98","content":"<p><math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It's given that the bar graph shows the number of students from one school who were born in either July, August, September, or October. The bar representing the number of students born in August has a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn></math>; therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn></math> students were born in August. The bar representing the number of students born in July has a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn></math>; therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn></math> students were born in July. Thus, there were <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"50 minus 40\"><mn>50</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> more students born in August than in July.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the total number of students born in July and August.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect. This is the number of students born in August.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the number of students born in July.</p>","externalid":"ad801a2d-5e09-4c92-b37a-9c8b027d62f2","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1755117017722,"updateDate":1755117017722}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017722, 1755117017722),
    ($SATQ$a0b165f8$SATQ$, $SATQ$71e0f3ea-a756-49f9-bc0d-dbe87bc5a198$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Percentages$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A scientist studying the life cycle of dragonflies counted the number of dragonflies in a certain habitat each day for <math alttext="46"><mn>46</mn>
</math> days. On February <math alttext="15"><mn>15</mn></math>, there were <math alttext="99"><mn>99</mn>
</math> dragonflies in the habitat. The percent increase in the number of dragonflies in the habitat from January <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math> to February <math alttext="15"><mn>15</mn></math> was <math alttext="12.50 percent sign"><mn>12.50</mn><mo>%</mo></math>. How many dragonflies were in the habitat on January <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"9897fc49-46e1-4937-946e-aa4ce09c0dcd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"88\"><mn>88</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1b15e7c4-f803-403e-8245-05069de44917","content":"<p><math alttext=\"87\"><mn>87</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"426c3038-5a1b-4195-a576-a59f8ce080c1","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"239d469c-6311-44ba-852a-1bd76a5e1ed2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["9897fc49-46e1-4937-946e-aa4ce09c0dcd"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that a scientist studying the life cycle of dragonflies counted the number of dragonflies in a certain habitat each day for <math alttext="46"><mn>46</mn>
</math> days. It&rsquo;s also given that on February <math alttext="15"><mn>15</mn>
</math>, there were <math alttext="99"><mn>99</mn>
</math> dragonflies in the habitat and that the percent increase in the number of dragonflies in the habitat from January <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> to February <math alttext="15"><mn>15</mn>
</math> was <math alttext="12.50 percent sign"><mn>12.50</mn><mo>%</mo></math>. This can be represented by the equation<br/><math alttext="99 equals left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction 12.50 Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis x"><mn>99</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>12.50</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi></math>, where <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> represents the number of dragonflies in the habitat on January <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>. This equation can be rewritten as <math alttext="99 equals 1.125 x"><mn>99</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1.125</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by&nbsp;<math alttext="1.125"><mn>1.125</mn></math> yields <math alttext="88 equals x"><mrow>
<mn>88</mn>
<mo>=</mo>
<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, there were <math alttext="88"><mn>88</mn>
</math> dragonflies in the habitat on January <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"a0b165f8","external_id":"71e0f3ea-a756-49f9-bc0d-dbe87bc5a198","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"da0505fd-727c-46b7-b78c-d4dca9a6593f","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.B.","skill_desc":"Percentages","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A scientist studying the life cycle of dragonflies counted the number of dragonflies in a certain habitat each day for <math alttext=\"46\"><mn>46</mn>\n</math> days. On February <math alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn></math>, there were <math alttext=\"99\"><mn>99</mn>\n</math> dragonflies in the habitat. The percent increase in the number of dragonflies in the habitat from January <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math> to February <math alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn></math> was <math alttext=\"12.50 percent sign\"><mn>12.50</mn><mo>%</mo></math>. How many dragonflies were in the habitat on January <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"9897fc49-46e1-4937-946e-aa4ce09c0dcd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"88\"><mn>88</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1b15e7c4-f803-403e-8245-05069de44917","content":"<p><math alttext=\"87\"><mn>87</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"426c3038-5a1b-4195-a576-a59f8ce080c1","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"239d469c-6311-44ba-852a-1bd76a5e1ed2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["9897fc49-46e1-4937-946e-aa4ce09c0dcd"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that a scientist studying the life cycle of dragonflies counted the number of dragonflies in a certain habitat each day for <mat